.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt RTIME 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rtime
.Nd time command execution
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ip
.Ar utility
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility executes and measures a command, printing its execution time and
system resource usage.
.Pp
The executed command is spawned via
.Xr posix_spawn 3 .
Upon completion,
.Nm
prints timing statistics alongside detailed metrics from
.Xr getrusage 2 ,
including resident set size, page faults, block I/O operations, and
context switches. When run on a supported RISC-V system, it also
prints the instructions retired, elapsed cycles, and execution speed
in MIPS.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i
Print detailed RISC-V CPU information before executing the
utility. This includes the current cycle and instruction counts, as
well as the supported base, single-letter, and Z-extensions.
.It Fl p
Enable CPU profiling. This flag writes a value of 1 to the custom
goemu CSR 0x802 before execution, and 0 upon completion.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr time 1 ,
.Xr getrusage 2 ,
.Xr posix_spawn 3
